# JobBeagle — Dual-Track Architecture (highest product priority)

Canonical detail: repo root **`.cursorrules`**. On conflict with older “call APIs freely” habits, **this dual-track wins**.

## Unit economics

- **Snapshot** = closed-book, Flash-Lite, **no** Google Search / web tools / scrape APIs.
- **Guide** = open-book, Pro (+ Search). Do not burn Pro/Search on Snapshot or free paths.
- Models: `constants/models.ts`. Analyze: `lib/gemini-analyze.ts`.

## Zero hallucination

- No invented experience, visas, employer offers, or uncitable “reported” interview Qs.
- Missing intel → `null` / limitations / validation questions — not fabricated facts.
- STAR / defenses: resume facts only.

## Track matrix (short)

| | Snapshot | Guide |
|--|----------|-------|
| Input | CV + JD | CV + JD + retrieval |
| Network | Forbidden | Grounding / Search OK |
| Offer band | Closed-book estimate only | Open-book compensation + Tier labels |
| Provenance | N/A | Required for cited web claims |

## Guide retrieval intents (order)

1. Business context (company / 12-mo facts)  
2. Interview intel (de-noise Glassdoor/Blind/public index)  
3. Market compensation (else Tier 3 baseline label)

May be one Pro+Search call today; semantics must stay.

## UI

- EvidenceBadge Tier 1 / 2 / 3; DefenseCard risk↔evidence; paywall for Guide depth.
- Report samples: always sync both products (see `jobbeagle-report-samples.mdc`).
